  "You'd have fifteen seconds, at most.",
  "What if you took off your helmet in space?",
  "First: you would not explode.",
  "Your skin is tough enough to hold you together.",
  "You would not freeze solid, either.",
  "A vacuum carries heat away very slowly.",
  "But the Sun's raw ultraviolet light would burn your skin.",
  "The real danger is your own breath.",
  "Hold it, and the air in your lungs expands and [tears](tairz) them.",
  "So you breathe out, and the clock starts.",
  "With no pressure, the water in your body starts turning to vapor.",
  "Your tissues swell, up to twice their normal size.",
  "In nineteen sixty, [Joe Kittinger's](Joe Kitt-in-jer's) pressure glove failed on a balloon flight.",
  "His hand swelled to about double its normal size.",
  "In nineteen sixty six, a NASA test suit leaked inside a vacuum chamber in Houston.",
  "[Jim LeBlanc](Jim luh-Blonk) felt the saliva on his tongue start to bubble.",
  "About fourteen seconds later, he passed out.",
  "The air rushed back in, and he woke up, with no lasting harm.",
  "In tests, dogs rescued within ninety seconds almost always survived.",
  "But after about two minutes, you'd likely be gone.",
  "That's about as long as brushing your teeth.",
  "So if your helmet ever comes off..."
